  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A COASTAL SOLUTIONS NETWORK FOR THE PACI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is the continuation of a network effort to implement the Pacific Americas Shorebird Conservation Strategy, with conservation actions in six priority sites (Mexico, Guatemala and Chile). Grantees will restore and manage 23,700 hectares through a combination of public policy mechanisms, restoration, and best management practices to reduce impacts on priority species of shorebirds. They will also build capacity for conservation leaders in Latin America and conduct outreach campaigns to create social support for these efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
